From: DuDuClaw OS Y7-1 (2026-08-26)
Subject: resolve CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDATADIR relative to the install prefix, not CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR

Real do_package_qa "buildpaths" failure hit by actually running
`bitbake fcitx5` (Y6-1's 4th round, picked up by Y7-1): "File
/usr/bin/fcitx5 in package fcitx5 contains reference to TMPDIR
[buildpaths]" (also libFcitx5Utils.so.5.1.12, its .debug split, and the
exported Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake -- see below). Root-caused by reading
the actual generated build/config.h, not guessing from the QA string
alone:

    #define FCITX_INSTALL_LIBDATADIR "<TMPDIR>/work/.../fcitx5-5.1.12/lib"

CMake's `get_filename_component(<out> <in> ABSOLUTE)` resolves a
*relative* input path against CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR when no BASE_DIR
is given (documented CMake behaviour, not a quirk). CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDATADIR
defaults to the *relative* value of CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR ("lib"), so the
call two lines below resolved "lib" against fcitx5's own source tree
root instead of the install prefix -- unlike every sibling
CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_* variable here (LIBDIR/INCLUDEDIR/LIBEXECDIR/DATADIR/
BINDIR), which all come from the standard GNUInstallDirs.cmake module and
correctly resolve against CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX. This is fcitx5's own
hand-rolled "libdata root (needed by bsd)" variable, introduced without
the BASE_DIR CMake already supports for exactly this case (available
since CMake 3.4, long predating this fcitx5 release -- confirmed by
`cmake --version` in this build's native sysroot).

FCITX_INSTALL_LIBDATADIR (set from this variable at CMakeLists.txt:211)
feeds two consumers, both of which leaked the same TMPDIR-rooted source
path:
  1. config.h.in -> config.h -> compiled as a literal C string constant
     wherever it's referenced (src/lib/fcitx-utils/standardpath.cpp),
     landing in libFcitx5Utils.so.5.1.12 and, transitively, /usr/bin/fcitx5.
  2. src/lib/fcitx-utils/Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake.in's
     FCITX_INSTALL_USE_FCITX_SYS_PATHS branch (line 23) -> the
     *exported* Fcitx5UtilsConfig.cmake that fcitx5-chewing's build
     consumes -- explaining the QA hit on that file specifically.

Fix: pass BASE_DIR "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}" so the relative "lib" input
resolves the same way CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDIR already does, producing
"${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/lib" (e.g. /usr/lib on this target) instead of
a source-tree path. Verified against the actual generated config.h after
rebuilding -- see the Y line TODO entry for the pass evidence, not
assumed from the patch alone.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet submitted to fcitx/fcitx5]
Signed-off-by: DuDuClaw OS Y7-1

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -199,7 +199,7 @@ if(NOT CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDATADIR)
   set(CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDATADIR "${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}" CACHE PATH "libdata root (LIBDIR)")
 endif()

-get_filename_component(CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDATADIR "${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDATADIR}" ABSOLUTE)
+get_filename_component(CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDATADIR "${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDATADIR}" ABSOLUTE BASE_DIR "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}")
 mark_as_advanced(CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDATADIR)
 mark_as_advanced(CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDATADIR)
